__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# uv.lock is NOT tracked. It only ever locks the `dev` convenience group in
# pyproject.toml -- the blessed checks in CONTRIBUTING.md bypass it
# (`--with pytest --with pytest-subtests` names its own deps), and the harness
# itself is stdlib-only, so nothing shipped is pinned by it. Worse, with no
# [project] table uv infers `requires-python` from whichever interpreter
# resolved first, so a regenerated lock can silently claim a floor nobody
# chose. Fewer moving parts than a lock that lies.
uv.lock
